0..72 Comment "//! Two terms that differ by the order of two arguments of a commutative"
73..100 Comment "//! operation are one term."
101..104 Comment "//!"
105..183 Comment "//! The theory of a tally states that its meet is commutative. A proof about a"
184..261 Comment "//! layout then needs `meet x y` and `meet y x` as one term. No rule fires on"
262..336 Comment "//! two arguments that are variables, so the rewriting does not join them."
337..340 Comment "//!"
341..417 Comment "//! The conversion pairs the two arguments of two meets in the written order"
418..491 Comment "//! or crossed. The checker records the crossed pairing in the trace. The"
492..569 Comment "//! kernel replays it only where its own rules hold the symmetry of the meet."
570..573 Comment "//!"
574..590 Comment "//! - see: #8311"
592..649 Comment "// `Tally`, its two rules that rewrite, and its symmetry."
